llama.cpp pin: 7fe450e19305b828c199d602c23a8337aaa1f03b (v0.5.0)

`third_party/llama.cpp` is checked out at this commit and nothing else. The app's
JNI engine is written against this revision's `common` chat-template and parser API,
so a bump is a code change, not a config change: rebuild, then re-run the native
parity tests before the pin moves.

To bump:

    git -C third_party/llama.cpp fetch --depth 1 origin <tag>
    git -C third_party/llama.cpp checkout <commit>
    git add third_party/llama.cpp

Update the SHA above in the same commit. A checkout of the superproject gets the
engine with `git submodule update --init --recursive`, which is what CI does.
